  "seoBody": "<div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>An environmental permit compliance audit checks a site against the conditions of its permit, condition by condition</li><li>In England and Wales most activities are permitted under the Environmental Permitting (England and Wales) Regulations 2016, enforced by the Environment Agency and NRW; SEPA runs the Scottish regime</li><li>The Environment Agency scores breaches by category and bands overall compliance, which feeds charges and enforcement</li><li>Finding and fixing your own breaches before the regulator does is cheaper than a scored non-compliance</li><li>Software does not make the site compliant; meeting the permit conditions does. The tool captures the audit and its evidence trail</li></ul></div><h2>What an environmental permit compliance audit is</h2><p>An environmental permit is a legal document and every condition in it is a duty. A compliance audit is the disciplined walk through those conditions to check the site is meeting each one, with evidence to prove it. Conditions typically cover emission limits, monitoring and sampling, record keeping, the waste types and quantities accepted, site infrastructure and containment, and management arrangements. The permit itself is the checklist.</p><p>Software does not make a site compliant. Meeting the permit conditions and the law does. What the tool does is capture what the officer found at each condition, with photo evidence, so a breach is visible before the regulator finds it. The record you complete on site, condition by condition, beats the one reconstructed from memory afterwards.</p><h2>The regulations and who enforces them</h2><p>Under the Environmental Permitting (England and Wales) Regulations 2016, operators of installations, waste operations, water discharges and other regulated activities hold a permit setting out how they must operate. The Environment Agency enforces in England and Natural Resources Wales in Wales. Scotland regulates equivalent activities under its own regime, enforced by SEPA. The requirements vary by nation and change over time, so audit against your own current permit and the regulator's live guidance, not a generic template. This is not legal advice.</p><h2>How compliance is scored</h2><p>The Environment Agency assesses permitted sites and classifies non-compliances by category, from minor administrative breaches to major ones with environmental impact. Those scores feed the site's compliance band and its annual subsistence charge, and a poor record can trigger enforcement. The purpose of an internal audit is to catch and close a breach before it becomes a scored one. The regulator, not the software, carries out the official assessment and sets the band.</p><h2>Records and duty of care</h2><p>Much of permit compliance is documentary: waste transfer notes and duty of care records under the waste duty of care in the Environmental Protection Act 1990, monitoring returns submitted on time, incident and complaint logs, and evidence the management system is being followed. A missing or late record is a breach even if the site itself is clean. An audit that only walks the yard misses half the risk.</p><h2>What to look for in permit audit software</h2><ul><li><strong>Condition-by-condition structure:</strong> the audit should follow the permit's conditions, not a generic template</li><li><strong>Photo evidence at the point of observation:</strong> each finding tied to a timestamped image of the plant, containment or document</li><li><strong>Open non-compliance visibility:</strong> the compliance manager should see open breaches on a dashboard, not buried in a filed PDF</li><li><strong>No per-seat penalty:</strong> per-seat pricing charges for office staff and subcontractor auditors who never file. Quickler is £20 per active user per month, dormant users free, everything unlimited</li><li><strong>Evidence trail:</strong> timestamp, officer, site, every condition checked, for the regulator inspection that surfaces later</li></ul><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Honest note:</strong> Quickler captures the audit and generates the report. It does not carry out the regulator's compliance assessment, set your compliance band, or replace legal advice. Meeting the permit conditions makes the site compliant. The competent person carries that judgement. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> if that distinction matters for your firm.</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is an environmental permit compliance audit?</h3><p>It is a structured check of a site against the conditions of its environmental permit, condition by condition, gathering evidence that each is being met. It covers emissions and monitoring, record keeping and duty of care, and site infrastructure such as containment. The permit itself is the checklist.</p><h3>Which regulations govern environmental permits in the UK?</h3><p>In England and Wales, most industrial and waste activities are permitted under the Environmental Permitting (England and Wales) Regulations 2016, enforced by the Environment Agency and Natural Resources Wales. Scotland runs its own regime enforced by SEPA. The requirements vary by nation and change over time, so audit against your own current permit and the regulator's live guidance. This is not legal advice.</p><h3>How does the Environment Agency assess compliance?</h3><p>The Environment Agency classifies non-compliances by category and bands a site's overall compliance, which feeds its subsistence charges and can trigger enforcement. An internal audit aims to find and close breaches before they become scored non-compliances. The regulator, not the software, carries out the official assessment.</p><h3>Can I run a permit compliance audit over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's workflow runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The officer receives each condition check in their existing WhatsApp chat, replies with text, a voice note or a photo, and the completed audit report generates automatically. No separate app or login is required, and Quickler manages the WhatsApp Business API account on the firm's behalf.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/environmental-inspection-software-uk.html\">Environmental inspection software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/spill-response-inspection-report-uk.html\">Spill response inspection report</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/iso-14001-audit-checklist-uk.html\">ISO 14001 audit checklist</a></li></ul>",
